{"id":45053,"ord":23,"n_segments":178,"prev":45052,"next":45054,"doc":{"id":"54270","title":"54270_Doc Cheatham oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Doc Cheatham","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/54270/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=54270"},"chapter":"Philadelphia, New York and Sam Wooding in Europe","title":"Philadelphia and Atlantic City clubs","category":"venue_city_scene","summary":"Philadelphia had many clubs and shows, such as the Standard Theater and the Paradise Club, and Atlantic City was jumping.","period":"1927","year_from":1927,"year_to":1927,"words":113,"start":[31,3],"end":[32,5],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=54270#s45053","tags":{"places":[{"name":"Philadelphia","focus":1,"type":"city"},{"name":"Atlantic City","focus":1,"type":"city"}],"venues":[{"name":"Horan's","focus":0,"city":"Philadelphia"},{"name":"The Madhouse","focus":0,"city":"Philadelphia"},{"name":"Standard Theater","focus":0,"city":"Philadelphia"},{"name":"Paradise Club","focus":0,"city":"Philadelphia"}],"bands":[]},"people":[{"name":"Gibson","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":37,"theme_name":"Gangsters, bootleggers and rough clubs of Prohibition","community":74,"community_name":"Cabarets, honky-tonks and the Storyville nightlife scene","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":31,"b":3,"s":"MR. ALBERTSON","x":"Well what was Philadelphia like in 1920 --"},{"p":31,"b":4,"s":"MR. CHEATHAM","x":"Philadelphia was very good. Very, very good. Many clubs with bands."},{"p":31,"b":5,"s":"MR. ALBERTSON","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":31,"b":6,"s":"MR. CHEATHAM","x":"All over the place and shows --"},{"p":31,"b":7,"s":"MR. ALBERTSON","x":"Do you remember, were they still open, there was a place called Horan's?"},{"p":31,"b":8,"s":"MR. CHEATHAM","x":"In Philadelphia?"},{"p":31,"b":9,"s":"MR. ALBERTSON","x":"Yeah."},{"p":31,"b":10,"s":"MR. CHEATHAM","x":"I don't remember that. No. I don't remember that."},{"p":31,"b":11,"s":"MR. ALBERTSON","x":"The Madhouse?"},{"p":31,"b":12,"s":"MR. CHEATHAM","x":"I don't remember the Madhouse."},{"p":31,"b":13,"s":"MR. ALBERTSON","x":"I guess they may have been closed by then."},{"p":31,"b":14,"s":"MR. CHEATHAM","x":"Yeah."},{"p":31,"b":15,"s":"MR. ALBERTSON","x":"The Standard Theater was open?"},{"p":31,"b":16,"s":"MR. CHEATHAM","x":"The Standard Theater was open."},{"p":31,"b":17,"s":"MR. ALBERTSON","x":"Gibson?"},{"p":32,"b":0,"s":"MR. CHEATHAM","x":"Yes. A place called the Paradise Club."},{"p":32,"b":1,"s":"MR. ALBERTSON","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":32,"b":2,"s":"MR. CHEATHAM","x":"Used to play up there, go up there all the time."},{"p":32,"b":3,"s":"MR. ALBERTSON","x":"And I guess Atlantic City was jumping?"},{"p":32,"b":4,"s":"MR. CHEATHAM","x":"Atlantic City was jumping, oh yes."},{"p":32,"b":5,"s":"MR. ALBERTSON","x":"Yeah."}]}